WEBVTT

00:06.980 --> 00:09.730
<b>Nagata Stationary</b>

00:09.730 --> 00:12.450
<b>Rocket Paper</b>

00:09.730 --> 00:12.450
<b>Taiyo Crevasse</b>

00:19.480 --> 00:21.040
<i>Oh, this is...</i>

00:21.950 --> 00:24.960
<i>One of those times I actually 
have to call for an employee...</i>

00:22.160 --> 00:24.960
<i>Badump Badump</i>

00:22.160 --> 00:24.960
<i>Badump Badump</i>

00:28.760 --> 00:31.120
<i>No, it's okay. I can totally do this.</i>

00:31.120 --> 00:33.450
<i>I'm gonna call for them! As loud as I can!</i>

00:33.450 --> 00:34.990
<i>Ready, and...</i>

00:34.990 --> 00:35.940
Ex...

00:36.340 --> 00:39.210
...cuse... me...

00:41.440 --> 00:43.640
E-Excuse me...

00:43.920 --> 00:46.560
Um... E-Excuse...

00:45.160 --> 00:48.660
<i>For some reason, I always feel 
like crying at times like this.</i>

00:48.660 --> 00:51.660
Maybe I'll just return 
everything and go home.

00:53.300 --> 00:55.220
Ow, ow, ow...

00:55.220 --> 00:58.470
Sorry about that. Did I make you wait?

00:58.470 --> 00:59.080
Oh?

00:59.580 --> 01:02.460
Well, if it isn't the 
Momijiyamas' girl, Teru-chan!

01:02.460 --> 01:05.850
I haven't seen you in years!
You've gotten so big!

01:05.850 --> 01:07.400
Er, yes...

01:07.400 --> 01:10.730
You used to come here with 
Mei-chan all the time.

01:10.730 --> 01:13.960
Er... You seem well yourself, Chihiro-san.

01:13.960 --> 01:15.340
Ow, ow, ow!

01:15.340 --> 01:18.050
<b>Nagata Stationary</b>

01:16.150 --> 01:17.850
Or not...

01:18.010 --> 01:18.970
<b>Nagata Stationary</b>

02:49.020 --> 02:52.100
<b>Rocket Paper</b>

02:49.020 --> 02:52.100
<b>Taiyo Crevasse</b>

02:49.020 --> 02:54.360
<b><u>Episode 5
</u>Shine the Light</b>

02:50.080 --> 02:52.100
A-Are you all right?

02:52.640 --> 02:54.750
Actually, no, I'm not.

02:55.680 --> 02:58.780
Ow... Sorry about this.

02:58.780 --> 03:02.330
My lower back's killing me lately.

03:04.600 --> 03:08.840
A-Are you running this shop 
alone now, Chihiro-san?

03:08.840 --> 03:12.080
I sure am, ever since my husband passed.

03:13.100 --> 03:14.840
Oh, you hadn't heard?

03:15.120 --> 03:17.640
He passed from an illness
around three years ago.

03:17.640 --> 03:19.440
Ow...

03:19.830 --> 03:22.680
It sure is lonely running 
this shop on my own.

03:23.700 --> 03:29.770
He started this shop as a hobby, 
and now, it's all I've got left.

03:29.770 --> 03:35.040
But there ain't too may people nowadays 
who'll come to a little shop like this.

03:35.040 --> 03:39.190
<b>Gaa Gaa Glue</b>

03:35.490 --> 03:38.710
That just makes things even lonelier.

03:39.630 --> 03:42.180
No wonder my back's given up on me.

03:43.370 --> 03:44.700
Oh, no...

03:45.300 --> 03:49.700
So what brings you here today, 
Teru-chan? Just came on a whim?

03:49.960 --> 03:51.620
Ah, no...

03:55.680 --> 03:57.340
For some reason...

03:58.200 --> 04:01.770
Mt. Tanpopo just looked so nice today.

04:03.320 --> 04:07.600
And then I remembered there was a 
really nice painting of it in this shop.

04:08.200 --> 04:11.340
Ah, my husband painted that.

04:12.080 --> 04:15.440
He always did love mountains.

04:15.440 --> 04:18.520
We used to go climbing together every year.

04:19.000 --> 04:22.110
I kept climbing, even after I ended up alone,

04:22.500 --> 04:25.110
but I don't see that happening this year.

04:25.240 --> 04:26.320
Throb

04:25.360 --> 04:26.320
Hngh!

04:26.320 --> 04:30.380
Ow, ow, ow! My back! My back! My back!

04:26.320 --> 04:31.290
<b>Nagata Stationary</b>

04:26.320 --> 04:31.290
<b>Nagata Stationary</b>

04:28.160 --> 04:31.700
A-A-A-A-Are you okay?!

04:37.690 --> 04:41.460
<i>Maybe I wasn't noticing the 
things closest to me lately.</i>

04:42.460 --> 04:44.940
<i>I wonder if there's anything I can do.</i>

04:44.940 --> 04:48.800
<i>Then again, it's not like 
I can cure Chihiro-san...</i>

04:48.800 --> 04:51.130
Teru, is something troubling you?

04:52.750 --> 04:55.760
I really am a failure...

04:55.760 --> 04:59.650
I haven't been able to use my fire 
powers since that day, either.

05:00.680 --> 05:02.800
There's no need to rush things.

05:06.480 --> 05:08.340
Y-Yes?

05:09.840 --> 05:11.120
You're...

05:12.450 --> 05:13.480
Wait, who are you?

05:13.480 --> 05:14.660
It's me, stupid!

05:14.660 --> 05:16.400
That doesn't...

05:16.400 --> 05:20.590
Even in the deepest darkness where the light 
doesn't reach, Black will be by your side.

05:20.590 --> 05:24.970
The light that shines upon the hearts of this 
world is a black star that shines on this Earth.

05:26.360 --> 05:29.430
I'm the Black Cross Nurse: Lady Black!

05:30.020 --> 05:33.180
I'll never give up on life.

05:33.940 --> 05:34.630
What?

05:37.440 --> 05:38.440
Do you know who I am now?!

05:39.350 --> 05:42.690
Piltz-san! But why'd you come 
all the way from Switzerland?

05:42.920 --> 05:46.950
I <i>am</i> the one who treated you, 
so I came to see how you're doing!

05:44.390 --> 05:46.130
Oh, dear...

05:48.160 --> 05:49.440
Anyway...

05:50.700 --> 05:53.060
Could you let me in already?

05:53.060 --> 05:54.540
Oh, s-sure!

05:56.290 --> 05:57.550
Any pain?

05:57.550 --> 05:59.080
N-No, I'm fine.

05:59.330 --> 06:01.750
Okay. Anything feel off?

06:01.750 --> 06:02.710
Not really.

06:04.500 --> 06:07.660
Way to go, me. A perfect recovery.

06:07.660 --> 06:09.750
The power of healing is so beautiful.

06:09.750 --> 06:10.850
Healing...

06:12.100 --> 06:14.440
Piltz-san! I have a favor to ask!

06:14.440 --> 06:15.430
Huh? What?!

06:15.430 --> 06:16.830
Well, you see...

06:17.390 --> 06:21.690
Well, maybe not a favor... 
It's more like a request...

06:21.690 --> 06:22.730
What?!

06:22.900 --> 06:25.570
I'm going home now! Are you stupid?!

06:25.890 --> 06:28.610
Why would I listen to your request?!

06:28.610 --> 06:30.400
Just how stupid are you?!

06:31.280 --> 06:32.570
Hello!

06:32.570 --> 06:37.540
<b>Nagata Stationary</b>

06:33.070 --> 06:37.540
I'm an acquaintance of Teru-san, and I'm 
a nursing student. My name is Piltz.

06:37.540 --> 06:40.170
My, my, my. What brings you here?

06:40.170 --> 06:42.100
Teru-san told me all about you.

06:42.100 --> 06:44.110
I was hoping I could help out in some way.

06:44.110 --> 06:46.270
Oh, is that so?

06:46.270 --> 06:50.180
Well, you're too kind. There ain't 
much room, but come on in.

06:50.180 --> 06:51.760
Thank you very much.

06:51.760 --> 06:54.110
Piltz-san, thank you so much!

06:54.110 --> 06:57.420
I'm not doing this for you. Stop 
thanking me over and over already.

06:58.460 --> 07:02.780
It's not really good to use your 
hero powers for personal matters,

07:03.260 --> 07:05.770
but I'm not strong enough 
to be able to ignore her.

07:14.310 --> 07:19.080
I feel a bit bad having a young'un 
like you do this for me.

07:19.080 --> 07:22.830
Oh, please, don't worry. 
I love taking care of others.

07:23.300 --> 07:25.060
Say, Piltz-chan.

07:25.060 --> 07:26.020
Yes?

07:26.020 --> 07:30.510
If the pain does go away, should 
I still not climb the mountain?

07:31.090 --> 07:32.630
Mountain?

07:33.220 --> 07:36.570
It's a memorable place for 
my late husband and me.

07:36.570 --> 07:39.270
I was hoping I'd be able 
to climb it again someday.

07:39.640 --> 07:40.960
Is that impossible?

07:41.500 --> 07:43.400
Mountain climbing sounds great!

07:43.400 --> 07:46.020
Lack of exercise is the 
worst thing for your health.

07:46.400 --> 07:51.470
But I'm sure you'd feel anxious going 
by yourself, so we'll go with you.

07:51.470 --> 07:52.130
Huh?

07:52.530 --> 07:54.530
<b>Mt. Tanpopo Trail</b>

07:53.360 --> 07:54.530
Huh?!

07:55.410 --> 07:57.780
Huh?!

07:57.780 --> 07:59.650
What a lovely day!

07:59.650 --> 08:01.110
Truly.

08:01.110 --> 08:02.910
Uh...

08:04.340 --> 08:07.040
Hey, what's with that stupid look on your face?

08:07.040 --> 08:10.160
Er, I'm not great at outdoorsy activities.

08:10.160 --> 08:14.130
I think it's pretty obvious, but I'm an 
indoor person, or in other words, a shut-in.

08:14.130 --> 08:17.510
Whatever. Anyway, let's get going.

08:18.090 --> 08:20.270
Teru-chan, no need to push yourself.

08:20.270 --> 08:22.450
Okay... I'll do my best.

08:34.960 --> 08:37.490
Truly, though, it's like magic.

08:37.800 --> 08:40.260
My back doesn't hurt at all anymore.

08:40.260 --> 08:42.530
Don't get too overconfident now.

08:42.530 --> 08:44.460
P-Piltz-san...

08:48.060 --> 08:51.330
Do you go... hiking often?

08:52.240 --> 08:55.300
You seem used to this...

08:56.980 --> 09:00.000
Well, I used to go hiking every day.

09:00.000 --> 09:04.310
W-Wow... Then I guess you 
must love mountains...

09:04.310 --> 09:05.540
I hate them.

09:06.340 --> 09:09.020
I hate mountains and hiking.

09:09.580 --> 09:12.500
There were some people who laughed 
at me and said I couldn't do it,

09:12.500 --> 09:14.820
so I just wanted to prove them wrong.

09:15.350 --> 09:19.320
Wh-Why would they laugh at you?

09:22.910 --> 09:24.620
Are you bad at physical activity?

09:24.620 --> 09:27.120
Uh, yes. Of course.

09:27.420 --> 09:29.100
Do you like hiking?

09:29.100 --> 09:30.130
No...

09:30.360 --> 09:32.570
Do you think you can make it to the summit?

09:32.570 --> 09:35.630
No, um... I honestly don't.

09:35.630 --> 09:36.620
Huh?

09:38.860 --> 09:40.420
Let's go, Nagata-san!

09:41.430 --> 09:44.430
I'll tell you the answer if 
I see you up on the summit!

09:48.460 --> 09:49.220
Huh?

09:57.080 --> 10:00.450
P-Piltz-san... I-I'm here...

10:00.960 --> 10:03.410
So... About what you said earlier...

10:03.410 --> 10:03.950
Shh.

10:13.280 --> 10:16.160
We'll continue this someplace 
where we won't interrupt Nagata-san.

10:16.160 --> 10:17.670
O-Okay...

10:23.990 --> 10:25.930
You took way too long.

10:25.930 --> 10:27.860
What were you even doing?

10:27.860 --> 10:28.940
Th-Thank you...

10:33.360 --> 10:35.710
I-I thought I was going to die...

10:35.710 --> 10:36.870
You're not going to die!

10:36.870 --> 10:38.950
This mountain isn't even that big.

10:39.950 --> 10:44.150
S-So, um... The thing 
you mentioned earlier...

10:46.300 --> 10:47.950
You really want to know?

10:47.950 --> 10:50.210
It's not exactly a fun story.

10:50.450 --> 10:53.450
But it's just so weird...

10:58.670 --> 10:59.420
Huh?

11:00.020 --> 11:03.180
I lost both of my legs in 
an accident a while ago.

11:03.440 --> 11:06.110
B-But you made it up here 
without any issue...

11:06.110 --> 11:09.180
That's right. I went hiking 
every day so I could.

11:10.650 --> 11:12.860
No matter the country or place,

11:12.860 --> 11:17.240
there are always idiots who laugh at the 
challenges of those who seem weaker than them.

11:19.360 --> 11:22.950
The place where I grew up 
was surrounded by mountains.

11:23.790 --> 11:26.810
It felt as though the world 
was trying to trap me inside.

11:28.100 --> 11:32.160
It pissed me off because it felt 
like my limits were decided for me.

11:33.080 --> 11:35.920
That's why I jumped out with my own two legs.

11:37.170 --> 11:39.920
There's no mountain that I can't conquer.

11:40.980 --> 11:43.520
Even you were able to climb this mountain.

11:43.520 --> 11:45.430
You can probably have a 
little more confidence.

11:45.900 --> 11:48.680
Honestly... I'm a little impressed.

11:48.680 --> 11:49.810
Piltz-san...

11:50.810 --> 11:54.220
I said "a little"! You need to train more!

11:54.220 --> 11:55.580
You dummy! You weakling!

11:57.360 --> 11:59.690
Hey, you two.

12:00.230 --> 12:02.300
Ready to start heading down?

12:02.300 --> 12:04.200
Oh, sure!

12:09.160 --> 12:11.460
It truly is a lovely day.

12:11.750 --> 12:13.450
It is!

12:13.450 --> 12:16.150
Hey, what are you doing? 
We're gonna leave you behind!

12:16.150 --> 12:18.280
Um... okay!

12:25.840 --> 12:28.810
<b>Nagata Stationary</b>

12:26.440 --> 12:28.810
Thank you so much for today.

12:29.070 --> 12:31.560
Come by the shop every once in a while.

12:31.770 --> 12:34.110
Yes, I'll come visit soon.

12:34.110 --> 12:36.350
Good, good. Well, see ya later.

12:38.970 --> 12:39.880
Um...

12:40.570 --> 12:42.780
Thank you very much.

12:42.780 --> 12:44.570
I didn't do anything.

12:45.090 --> 12:45.940
No, really.

12:45.940 --> 12:52.040
It's very clear that you're able to help 
and heal others even without your powers.

12:53.600 --> 12:56.710
Why did you have to go and 
state the obvious like that?

12:57.650 --> 12:59.210
I-I mean...

12:59.450 --> 13:04.720
I guess I wouldn't mind helping 
you become a proper hero.

13:05.300 --> 13:05.960
Huh?

13:06.470 --> 13:08.790
I'm worried about Nagata-san's progress, too,

13:08.790 --> 13:10.720
so I might just be back after a while!

13:11.250 --> 13:12.540
Well, bye!

13:15.120 --> 13:16.770
<i>I wonder if I'll...</i>

13:17.220 --> 13:19.150
<i>be able to conquer a mountain, too.</i>

13:22.770 --> 13:23.540
Shy!

13:25.530 --> 13:28.990
<u>Real Name: Piltz Dunant
Nationality: Swiss
Likes: Volunteer work, black things
A hero from the international rescue
organization Black Cross</u>

13:37.150 --> 13:38.040
Fire!

13:41.460 --> 13:43.960
<b>Silence</b>

13:44.320 --> 13:46.300
You'll be late for school, Teru.

13:47.550 --> 13:50.350
D-Don't watch my secret training!

13:55.040 --> 14:00.470
<i>Piltz-san was able to use her healing 
powers even without Heart-shifting.</i>

14:01.410 --> 14:05.440
<i>I wonder how I can use my 
heart's power efficiently...</i>

14:05.440 --> 14:07.320
Morning, Momijiyama-san!

14:08.160 --> 14:09.280
Momijiyama-san?

14:10.290 --> 14:13.400
O-Oh, Koishikawa-san, good morning...

14:13.400 --> 14:14.790
O-Oh, and...

14:15.530 --> 14:17.030
Your uniform...

14:17.030 --> 14:21.000
Oh, this? They finally sent 
me this school's uniform.

14:22.750 --> 14:25.050
It looks great on you! So cute!

14:26.530 --> 14:28.460
Anyway, is something wrong?

14:28.460 --> 14:29.770
Something on your mind?

14:29.770 --> 14:31.380
I'll help out any way I can.

14:31.380 --> 14:32.640
Er, no...

14:32.990 --> 14:35.260
<i>This is hard to bring up to Koishikawa-san</i>

14:35.260 --> 14:38.770
<i>after I embarrassingly said I'd 
get stronger the other day...</i>

14:39.420 --> 14:40.940
Morning, Koishikawa-san.

14:40.940 --> 14:42.160
Morning!

14:42.160 --> 14:43.820
Morning, Momijiyama-san.

14:43.820 --> 14:45.530
M-Morning...

14:45.830 --> 14:48.680
Koishikawa-san, you look great 
in our school's uniform.

14:48.680 --> 14:49.980
Is your leg okay now?

14:49.980 --> 14:52.870
Oh, yeah. It's okay right now.

14:54.250 --> 14:57.920
<i>Anyway, I need to hurry and 
learn how to use my powers.</i>

15:00.920 --> 15:02.000
<i>Fire...</i>

15:02.000 --> 15:05.000
Science Room

15:02.500 --> 15:05.000
Beware
of
fire

15:03.230 --> 15:05.000
<i>Fire...</i>

15:06.290 --> 15:07.130
<i>Fire!</i>

15:07.800 --> 15:08.980
<i>Fire...</i>

15:08.980 --> 15:09.800
<i>Fire...</i>

15:09.800 --> 15:11.070
<i>Fire?</i>

15:11.070 --> 15:12.700
<i>Fire...</i>

15:17.320 --> 15:20.940
<i>I couldn't concentrate on 
my classes at all today.</i>

15:21.210 --> 15:23.490
You're not heading home, Momijiyama-san?

15:23.490 --> 15:24.940
Oh, uh...

15:25.180 --> 15:27.710
I-I thought I'd stay after school a bit.

15:27.710 --> 15:30.450
Oh, okay... Well, see you tomorrow, then.

15:34.640 --> 15:37.240
<i>I can't afford to make 
Koishikawa-san worry right now.</i>

15:37.690 --> 15:40.250
<i>I need to get this down on my own.</i>

15:42.850 --> 15:45.840
<i>Fire... Flames...</i>

15:45.840 --> 15:47.520
<i>Burning...</i>

15:49.630 --> 15:51.930
<b>Flame</b>

15:55.760 --> 15:59.290
<i>This character that means 
"flame" seems warm somehow...</i>

15:59.900 --> 16:03.160
<i>Wait, are flames hotter than fire?</i>

16:03.160 --> 16:06.040
<i>Um... What's the difference 
between fire and flames, anyway?</i>

16:06.040 --> 16:10.570
<i>Are they just different in size? Actually, 
maybe it doesn't even matter...</i>

16:10.570 --> 16:12.370
You need something?

16:18.020 --> 16:23.750
Um, no, I... was just thinking this 
"flame" was written very nicely!

16:25.160 --> 16:27.880
This is one that I wrote.

16:28.340 --> 16:30.380
Do you want to check out 
the calligraphy club?

16:30.380 --> 16:31.630
Er, no, I...

16:32.070 --> 16:33.630
Stare...

16:34.220 --> 16:35.530
Uh, okay...

16:35.390 --> 16:36.640
The type 
of girl
who can't 
say no

16:37.680 --> 16:38.640
President.

16:38.640 --> 16:41.140
<i>I don't have time for this...</i>

16:41.730 --> 16:43.140
Wait one sec.

17:00.620 --> 17:01.600
There.

17:04.540 --> 17:05.690
Who's that?

17:06.120 --> 17:07.330
She wanted to observe.

17:07.330 --> 17:10.500
Huh?! Observe?! But why our club?!

17:10.880 --> 17:13.250
She said she liked my calligraphy.

17:13.250 --> 17:14.100
Y-Yes...

17:14.100 --> 17:15.510
So she's not a bad person.

17:16.660 --> 17:20.700
Well, everyone's welcome 
here, so enjoy yourself.

17:22.350 --> 17:23.310
Okay...

17:23.310 --> 17:24.810
The type 
of girl 
who
 can't turn
 back

17:26.230 --> 17:27.730
<b>Natural</b>

17:32.480 --> 17:35.540
<i>Her posture's so nice when 
she's about to write.</i>

17:35.540 --> 17:38.820
So why did you like the "flame" calligraphy?

17:38.820 --> 17:40.680
U-Um...

17:40.680 --> 17:43.520
You don't seem like someone 
well-versed in this.

17:43.520 --> 17:46.330
Er, I honestly have no idea why...

17:46.330 --> 17:51.710
<b>Champion | Flame | Life</b>

17:46.760 --> 17:50.440
but that character just caught 
my eye when I was walking by.

17:50.440 --> 17:54.980
Somehow, it felt like it had 
actual heat coming from it...

17:51.710 --> 17:57.470
<b>Flame</b>

17:51.710 --> 17:57.470
<b>Suzuri 
Murasaki</b>

17:54.980 --> 17:57.470
Huh... That's an interesting 
way of putting it.

17:57.810 --> 17:59.660
I-Is it weird?

18:00.660 --> 18:04.170
No, I think that's actually pretty common.

18:04.170 --> 18:07.360
She might not seem very motivated,

18:07.360 --> 18:10.110
but her calligraphy is 
very delicate yet bold.

18:10.110 --> 18:11.290
It's very passionate.

18:11.840 --> 18:14.480
What you're feeling inside shows 
in the characters you write.

18:16.330 --> 18:17.980
You guys are too noisy.

18:17.980 --> 18:20.830
Uh... You're the one who invited her in.

18:20.830 --> 18:23.910
You two keep yammering on about 
stuff that doesn't matter.

18:25.370 --> 18:26.330
<b>Passion</b>

18:26.980 --> 18:27.930
What do you think?

18:28.350 --> 18:30.700
It's good. Maybe concentrate 
on balance more next time.

18:30.700 --> 18:31.330
'Kay.

18:31.980 --> 18:33.120
What do you think?

18:33.120 --> 18:33.750
Huh?!

18:34.430 --> 18:39.760
I don't know all this stuff in detail, 
but your writing seems warm,

18:40.080 --> 18:42.230
so I really like it a lot.

18:42.230 --> 18:43.760
'Kay. Thanks.

18:45.140 --> 18:47.280
You're so happy.

18:47.280 --> 18:49.270
Shut up.

18:51.400 --> 18:54.310
Wanna give it a try? 
Since you're here and all.

18:54.310 --> 18:56.220
Huh? Uh, I...

18:57.410 --> 19:00.390
You should try everything.

19:02.620 --> 19:04.030
<i>I'm so...</i>

19:04.950 --> 19:06.950
<b>

19:06.950 --> 19:09.370
<b>Crimson</b></b>

19:14.040 --> 19:19.260
<b>Teru</b>

19:14.730 --> 19:17.980
I-I think this turned out pretty well.

19:17.630 --> 19:19.260
The type of
 girl that ends 
up enjoying 
anything in the end

19:19.260 --> 19:22.640
Yeah, there's passion in your calligraphy, too.

19:22.640 --> 19:23.310
Yeah.

19:23.310 --> 19:25.010
Y-You think so?

19:25.010 --> 19:26.970
This is my pet theory,

19:26.970 --> 19:31.020
but I think calligraphy cherishes your 
heart more than any other art form.

19:31.840 --> 19:33.670
Your... heart?

19:33.670 --> 19:34.190
Yeah.

19:36.710 --> 19:38.310
You only have one brush,

19:38.310 --> 19:40.510
and there are no redos in this world,

19:40.510 --> 19:43.020
so you focus all you have 
into this one moment.

19:43.680 --> 19:47.430
The thing you want to express from 
your heart passes through your arm,

19:47.430 --> 19:49.040
and then, through the brush,

19:49.510 --> 19:52.000
it becomes a character on the paper.

19:52.780 --> 19:55.500
The character born of these 
momentary flicks of the wrist

19:56.960 --> 19:59.110
can be called the heart itself.

19:57.840 --> 19:59.760
<b>Heart</b>

20:03.340 --> 20:05.070
That's it!

20:06.020 --> 20:09.400
That's right. If I want 
my heart to come out...

20:09.400 --> 20:11.350
If I go with this image, 
I might just be able to...

20:11.700 --> 20:13.700
Um, I'm going home now!

20:13.700 --> 20:14.340
Huh?!

20:14.340 --> 20:16.920
Thank you for everything today, you two.

20:16.920 --> 20:17.610
Uh, sure.

20:20.750 --> 20:22.480
What got into her?

20:22.480 --> 20:23.140
Oh.

20:23.140 --> 20:24.240
Huh? What?

20:24.240 --> 20:30.750
<b>Teru</b>

20:24.610 --> 20:27.050
I forgot to ask her what her name was.

20:27.050 --> 20:29.670
Actually, we didn't introduce 
ourselves, either...

20:39.520 --> 20:41.840
Teru... What are you doing?

20:42.360 --> 20:45.090
I'm going to... write out my heart.

20:46.740 --> 20:49.300
<i>That's right... I can't be reckless.</i>

20:49.720 --> 20:51.520
<i>I need to concentrate on 
writing this character.</i>

20:52.410 --> 20:55.790
<i>Like I'm creating an image 
and writing my heart out.</i>

20:56.740 --> 20:58.960
<i>How do I feel right now?</i>

20:59.500 --> 21:00.600
<i>Am I panicked?</i>

21:01.030 --> 21:02.380
<i>Scared?</i>

21:07.240 --> 21:10.480
<i>I need to imagine it over and over...</i>

21:11.790 --> 21:14.790
<i>No matter how I'm feeling...</i>

21:16.330 --> 21:18.170
<i>I just need to write it out.</i>

21:18.170 --> 21:19.460
<b>Fire</b>

21:22.590 --> 21:24.840
<b>Fire</b>

21:24.840 --> 21:26.720
<b>Fire</b>

21:28.870 --> 21:31.140
<i>I did it!</i>

21:31.470 --> 21:33.760
<i>I guess even I can do it if I try.</i>

21:33.760 --> 21:35.640
<i>I'm glad I gave it my all.</i>

21:35.640 --> 21:37.050
Teru. Teru!

21:37.950 --> 21:39.200
It's actually on fire!

21:39.200 --> 21:40.360
Huh?!

21:40.360 --> 21:42.880
Oh, no! Shrimpy-san! Water! Water!

21:42.880 --> 21:43.550
Huh?

21:44.080 --> 21:44.900
Huh?

23:19.960 --> 23:21.210
<b>Extra</b>

23:21.670 --> 23:23.630
<b>Proclaiming your
 name is 
pretty great.</b>

23:22.500 --> 23:23.630
<b>Nice</b>

23:23.630 --> 23:26.460
<b>You have
 nothing to 
proclaim?</b>

23:24.630 --> 23:26.460
<b>You're 
Japan's 
hero, 
aren't 
you?</b>

23:25.460 --> 23:26.460
<b>Er, I...</b>

23:26.460 --> 23:29.630
<b>Well, 
I'm 
sh-shy...</b>

23:27.300 --> 23:29.630
<b>Well?</b>

23:27.550 --> 23:29.630
<b>Too embarrassing, 
too embarrassing...</b>

23:28.420 --> 23:29.630
<b>Hurry it up!</b>

23:29.970 --> 23:32.760
<b>I'm alive, but 
it's embarrassing!</b>

23:30.800 --> 23:32.760
<b>The living-embarrassment 
Shy has arrived!</b>

23:31.680 --> 23:32.760
<b><i>Baaam</i></b>

23:33.800 --> 23:35.100
Wooo

23:35.350 --> 23:37.010
<b>Are you 
stupid?</b>

23:35.970 --> 23:37.180
<b>Don't make me smack you</b>

23:36.220 --> 23:36.970
<b>So mean!</b>
